<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tequesta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tequesta were an Indigenous people of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, living around Biscayne Bay and the mouth of the Miami River. They fished, hunted and gathered, and were at times tributary to the Calusa. The Spanish set up a short-lived mission among them in 1567, and disease and slave raids led to their disappearance in the 18th century; the Miami Circle is attributed to them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tequesta.jpg" alt="Tequesta" width="300" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dalbury at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FLMap-Tequesta-tribe2.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
